---
// The dogfooding page (#812 (website redo 3/4)): the tower of paros
// primitives that paros runs on, and under it a live run of the playground
// engine with an x-ray: each layer's traffic, read from the run's events and
// from the topology the admin API reports (public/engineering.js).
import Doc from "../../layouts/Doc.astro";
import Panel from "../../components/Panel.astro";
import { url } from "../../nav";

const LAYERS = [
  {
    num: "01", title: "cell init", flavor: "single-decree Paxos",
    what: "The founding machines choose the cell plan once: the members, the cell's ids and its first matchmaker set. Before it, nothing is elected, so the decree is the first election.",
    code: ["paros-core/src/decree.rs", "paros-machine/src/wait.rs"],
    paxos: "paxos/single-decree/",
  },
  {
    num: "02", title: "cell/election · cell/control", flavor: "Multi-Paxos · leader election",
    what: "Two journals of the cell tenant. The election journal elects the cell coordinator; the winner claims cell/control with SetLeader. cell/control holds the machine registry and the capacity bookings.",
    code: ["paros-client/src/election.rs", "paros-coordinator/src/cell.rs"],
    paxos: "paxos/multi-paxos/",
  },
  {
    num: "03", title: "universe/control", flavor: "Multi-Paxos",
    what: "The universe directory: which cell hosts which tenant. The universe coordinator writes it; every index under it can be built again from the tenant control journals.",
    code: ["paros-coordinator/src/universe.rs", "paros-client/src/universe.rs"],
    paxos: "paxos/multi-paxos/",
  },
  {
    num: "04", title: "tenant control journals", flavor: "Multi-Paxos · Matchmaker Paxos",
    what: "One per tenant: its name, its journals, their durability and placement, and its desired state. The tenant coordinator reads it and places the journals.",
    code: ["paros-coordinator/src/tenant.rs", "paros-model/src/tenant.rs"],
    paxos: "paxos/matchmaker/",
  },
  {
    num: "05", title: "user journals", flavor: "Multi-Paxos · Compartmentalized · quorums",
    what: "What the clients write and read, with the four calls. Each journal has its own acceptors, matchmakers and quorum system.",
    code: ["paros-roles/src/node.rs", "paros-client/src/writer.rs"],
    paxos: "paxos/compartmentalized/",
  },
];
---
<Doc title="paros on paros" kicker="Engineering" section="engineering/" widget
  description="The control plane of paros is made of paros: journals, elections and Paxos flavors. There is no external coordination service. Pull the layers apart and see the traffic of each one.">
    <h2>The tower</h2>
    <p>A cell needs a membership, a coordinator, a directory of tenants and the description of each
      tenant. paros keeps all of them in its own journals, on the same machines, with the same Paxos,
      the same stores and the same <code>Write</code> call as a user's journal. There is no special path
      and no external service such as ZooKeeper or etcd. Each layer stands on the layer under it.</p>

  <div class="xray" data-widget="xray">
    <div class="tower" role="list" aria-label="The layers of paros, from the base up">
      {LAYERS.map((l) => (
        <div class="layer" role="listitem" data-layer={Number(l.num)}>
          <Panel num={l.num} title={l.title} meta={l.flavor}>
            <p class="layer-what">{l.what}</p>
            <p class="layer-code label">
              {l.code.map((c) => <code>{c}</code>)}
              <a href={url(l.paxos)}>the flavor →</a>
            </p>
            <div class="layer-traffic"><p class="aside">A live run draws this layer's traffic here. It needs JavaScript and the playground engine.</p></div>
          </Panel>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

    <h2>Read the x-ray</h2>
    <p>The run above is the <a href={url("playground/")}>playground</a> engine: five <code>parosd</code>
      machines on a simulated network, disk and clock, in your browser. Each bar is the traffic of a
      layer over the simulated time of the run. Press <b>x-ray</b> on a layer to show only its traffic
      and its message kinds. The page reads the layers from the run's events and from the admin
      <code>Inspect</code> of each journal: a read only, it changes nothing in the run.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Layer 01 talks once, at the start, and then never again.</li>
      <li>Layers 02 to 04 keep a leader with heartbeats and lease reads even when nothing changes.
        Show the heartbeats to see them.</li>
      <li>Layer 05 moves only when a client writes or reads.</li>
      <li>Crash a machine: the layers that had a leader on it elect a new one, with the same code.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>One thing to run.</strong> The control plane fails, recovers and scales like the data
        plane, because it is the data plane.</li>
      <li><strong>One thing to test.</strong> Every simulation run tests the control plane with the same
        faults, the same audit and the same linearizability checker as user journals.</li>
      <li><strong>The flavors earn their place.</strong> A control journal is a hard user of paros: few
        writes, many readers, a leader that must never be two.</li>
    </ul>
</Doc>
